  "last_executor_claim": "Report written to `/app/report.md`. All 17 cited doc IDs verified against `index.json`; input files untouched.\n\nWhat's in it:\n\n- **Overview** — adoption is broad (88% org AI use) but mostly pilot-stage; ~$4.4T long-term opportunity per McKinsey; unprecedented infrastructure capex (Stargate up to $500B, Microsoft ~$80B, Nvidia–OpenAI ~$100B) large enough to affect US GDP (D0074, D0191, D0167).\n- **Startup examples** — VoiceRun ($5.5M seed, voice agents), Symbolic.ai (News Corp deal), MergeLabs ($250M seed at $850M valuation), plus the healthcare AI cluster and AI Fund portfolio (D0040, D0069, D0009, D0112).\n- **Health/direction** — bullish usage/funding signals vs. credible bubble warnings (17× dotcom-era investment levels, circular vendor financing, only 39% reporting enterprise EBIT impact) (D0074, D0079, D0167).\n- **Economic/regulatory flags** — fragmented global AI regulation, EU AI Act transparency tiers, bubble-correction risk, IP/licensing litigation, shifting US tech-policy posture (D0148, D0050, D0079, D0186).\n- **Projections read-through** — the 8× revenue ramp, flat 74% gross margin, and declining CAC are plausible narratives but not directly benchmarkable in this corpus; flagged where investors will probe.\n- **Limitations** — tex.pdf is a placeholder template (so scope = general AI industry); no direct AI market-size figure exists in the corpus (adjacent tech-market CAGRs used instead); corpus is a mixed-quality scrape concentrated in ~15 substantive docs.",
